From bcbe31fd8ebb611bf944bd9bab7ffd5f41342994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:01:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a card placed from a chat carries that
 chat's created link to the Board from its owner, so the chat sees it while
 its own Board sync is stopped

The courier create/adopt (kanban_origin_creation) wrote only the owner's hub sub for the origin chat, so the
chat's task_chat_links row came only from the origin's ledger reconcile, pushed by the origin's sync. With that
sync given up (SchemaAhead, laptop-1 2026-11-13 01:09 PT) four placed cards had 0 Board link rows and the chat
never listed them. The owner now writes the same-uid created link in the create transaction (as
initialize_ownership already does for --origin-session), skipping a chat on the owner, a placement placeholder
and an unproven local-<sha256> hash (only the chat's gateway can tell a Desktop chat from a worker's own hash).
On recovery the origin's reconcile writes the same uid: one Board row.

kanban_create notes a placed create while this gateway's sync is stopped as chat_link: owner_written (the
link is on the Board; only this replica lags); chat_link: queued_local stays for a local-<sha256> chat the owner
writes no link for.
